    <h2>Make your own version (the legal way)</h2>
    <p>Everything that makes the format work — the loop structure, the booth look, the call-and-response trade — is describable in original prompt words, and none of it requires the audio or faces any specific viral clip used. The recipe: two consented photos, the <a href="/prompts/ai-rap-video-duo-prompt/">duo prompt</a> with its stage block swapped for the <a href="/ai-rap-video-orange-backdrop/">orange look</a>, original bars from the <a href="/prompts/ai-rap-video-original-lyrics-prompt/">lyrics template</a>, and a 9:16 render from the <a href="/prompts/ai-rap-video-vertical-tiktok-prompt/">vertical template</a> if it is headed for TikTok. The full walkthrough is the <a href="/how-to-make-ai-rap-video/">10-step workflow</a>.</p>

    <h2>Beat breakdown: why 8-12 seconds</h2>
    <ol class="list">
      <li><strong>0-2s — Hook-first.</strong> The establishing shot doubles as the hook; feed viewers decide here.</li>
      <li><strong>2-9s — The trade.</strong> Bars alternate on the locked frame; lip-sync credibility lives or dies here.</li>
      <li><strong>9-12s — The loop point.</strong> A push-in to a clean hold that cuts back to frame one. Seamless loops masquerade as longer watch time, which is exactly the point.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Negative prompts</h2>
    <p>The trend's failure modes are the trend's copies: backdrop drift, identity swaps, karaoke text overlays, and stray brand logos from whatever the model associate's with "rap video." The standard block covers all four — <a href="/prompts/ai-rap-video-negative-prompt-guide/">category-organized here</a> — with the orange-specific additions in the <a href="/ai-rap-video-orange-backdrop/">backdrop guide</a>.</p>

    <h2>Photo prep and common failures</h2>
    <ul class="list">
      <li><strong>Background contrast.</strong> Source photos against busy or warm backgrounds fight the booth look; neutral backgrounds composite cleanest.</li>
      <li><strong>Safe-area heads.</strong> Feed UI crops tops of frames; the vertical template bakes headroom into the framing.</li>
      <li><strong>Face drift</strong> is the universal failure — diagnose by symptom with the <a href="/prompts/ai-rap-video-troubleshooting-faces/">troubleshooting guide</a> instead of rewriting the prompt blind.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="notice"><strong>Compliance:</strong> the visual grammar is a generic convention; the specific commercial recordings, specific music videos, and real people's faces are not yours to bind. Original lyrics and staging only — the <a href="/ai-rap-video-vs-hotel-lobby-trend/">compliance comparison</a> holds the full line.</div>

